Falsifies `globally_unique_identifier_partition_table::verification::an_entry_survives_the_round_trip`.

The defect: `Entry::encode` writes the UTF-16 name units big-endian where `decode` reads them little-endian.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert_eq!(Entry::decode(&bytes).encode(), bytes)`.

diff --git a/crates/globally_unique_identifier_partition_table/src/entry.rs b/crates/globally_unique_identifier_partition_table/src/entry.rs
index 04d4270c8..595f342c2 100644
--- a/crates/globally_unique_identifier_partition_table/src/entry.rs
+++ b/crates/globally_unique_identifier_partition_table/src/entry.rs
@@ -181,3 +181,3 @@ impl Entry {
             let o = at::NAME + i * 2;
-            bytes[o..o + 2].copy_from_slice(&unit.to_le_bytes());
+            bytes[o..o + 2].copy_from_slice(&unit.to_be_bytes());
         }
